The expression for the vertical stress [latex]\left(\sigma_{2}\right)[/latex] at any point [latex](r, z)[/latex] with the half-space is given as [latex]\sigma_{z}=\frac{3 P}{2 \pi} \frac{z^{3}}{\left(r^{2}+z^{2}\right)^{5 / 2}}
[/latex] For [latex]\sigma_{\mathrm{z}}[/latex] to be maximum [latex]\begin{aligned}
& \frac{\sigma_{z}}{\partial z}=0 \Rightarrow \frac{3 P}{2 \pi} \frac{\partial}{\partial z}\left[\frac{z^{3}}{\left(r^{2}+z^{2}\right)^{5 / 2}}\right] \\
&=\frac{3 P}{2 \pi} \frac{\left[\left(r^{2}+z^{2}\right)^{5 / 2}-z^{3} \times \frac{5}{2}\left(r^{2}+z^{2}\right)^{3 / 2} \times 2 z\right]}{\left(r^{2}+z^{2}\right)^{5}}=0 \\
&=\left[\left(r^{2}+z^{2}\right)\left(3 z^{2}\right)-5 z^{4}\right]=0 \\
&=3 r^{2}+3 z^{2}=5 z^{2} \\
& z^{2}=\frac{3 r^{2}}{2}
\end{aligned}
[/latex]

