Given: Diffusion equation: [latex]
\frac{\partial T}{\partial t}=\mathrm{D} \frac{\partial^{2} \mathrm{~T}}{\partial \mathrm{x}^{2}}
[/latex] And also, [latex]D=1[/latex] [latex]\mathrm{T}(0, \mathrm{t})=0[/latex] [latex]\mathrm{T}(5,5)=0[/latex] [latex]T(x, 0)=T_{0}[/latex] We know, solution of equation is given by, [latex]T(x, t)=\left(C_{1} \cos \alpha x+C_{2} \sin \alpha x\right) C_{3} e^{-\alpha^{2} t} \;\;\; ...(1)[/latex] For [latex]\mathrm{T}(0, t)=0[/latex] [latex]\left(C_{1}+0\right) C_{3} e^{-\alpha^{2} t}=0[/latex] [latex]\Rightarrow \mathrm{C}_{1}=0[/latex] For [latex]\mathrm{T}(\mathrm{s}, \mathrm{t})=0[/latex] [latex]\left(C_{2} \sin \alpha 5\right) C_{3} \mathrm{e}^{-25 t}=0[/latex] [latex]\Rightarrow \sin 5 \alpha=0[/latex] [latex]\Rightarrow \alpha=\frac{\mathrm{n} \pi}{5}[/latex] Now, from equation (1) [latex]T(x, t)=C_{2} C_{3} \sin \left(\frac{n \pi x}{5}\right) e^{-\frac{n^{2} \pi^{2}}{25} t}[/latex] [latex]=b_{n} \sin \left(\frac{n \pi x}{5}\right) e^{-\frac{n^{2} \pi^{2} t}{25}}[/latex] Generalize solution [latex]T(x, t)=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} b_{n} \sin \left(\frac{n \pi x}{5}\right) e^{-\frac{n^{2} \pi^{2} t}{25}}[/latex] For [latex]\mathrm{T}(\mathrm{x}, 0)=\mathrm{T}_{0}[/latex] [latex]\Rightarrow T_{0}=\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} b_{n} \sin \left(\frac{n \pi x}{5}\right)[/latex] From fourier series, [latex]b_{n}=0[/latex] for even value of [latex]n[/latex] [latex]\therefore \mathrm{T}(\mathrm{x}, \mathrm{t})=\sum_{\mathrm{n}=13,5 \ldots .}^{\infty} \mathrm{b}_{\mathrm{n}} \sin \left(\frac{\mathrm{n} \pi \mathrm{x}}{5}\right) \mathrm{e}^{-\frac{\mathrm{n}^{2} \pi^{2} \mathrm{t}}{25}}[/latex] Given: [latex]T(x, t)=\sum_{n=13,5 \ldots .}^{\infty} C_{n} \sin \left(\frac{n \pi x}{5}\right) e^{-\beta n^{2} t}[/latex] On comparison; [latex]\beta=\frac{\pi^{2}}{25}=0.395 \mathrm{sec}^{-1}[/latex]
